@* Shown when the Blazor Server circuit drops. Without it the app has no reconnection UI whatsoever: the
   websocket goes away, the framework retries silently, and the page just stops responding to input with
   nothing on screen to say why. That is a routine event here, not an edge case — this app sits behind
   Cloudflare on a home server, so a sleeping laptop or a wifi blip is enough.

   The element ids and class names are a contract with the framework: blazor.web.js dispatches
   `components-reconnect-state-changed` at this element and toggles the classes the stylesheet keys off.
   Renaming any of them silently disables the modal, which is how it fails without an error. *@

<script type="module" src="@Assets["Components/Layout/ReconnectModal.razor.js"]"></script>

<dialog id="components-reconnect-modal" data-nosnippet>
    <div class="components-reconnect-container">
        <div class="components-rejoining-animation" aria-hidden="true">
            <div></div>
            <div></div>
        </div>
        <p class="components-reconnect-first-attempt-visible">
            Reconnecting to the server…
        </p>
        @* "in <n>s" rather than the template's "in <n> seconds", which reads "in 1 seconds" on the last
           tick before each retry — the framework injects a bare number and there's no hook to pluralise. *@
        <p class="components-reconnect-repeated-attempt-visible">
            Reconnect failed — retrying in <span id="components-seconds-to-next-attempt"></span>s.
        </p>
        <p class="components-reconnect-failed-visible">
            Couldn't reconnect.<br />Retry, or reload the page.
        </p>
        <button id="components-reconnect-button" class="components-reconnect-failed-visible">
            Retry
        </button>
        <p class="components-pause-visible">
            The session was paused by the server.
        </p>
        <p class="components-resume-failed-visible">
            Couldn't resume the session.<br />Retry, or reload the page.
        </p>
        <button id="components-resume-button" class="components-pause-visible components-resume-failed-visible">
            Resume
        </button>
    </div>
</dialog>
